st "the same mechanism happening more times." No matter how many pages you feed through your home printer, it will never start operating like a rolling press — the volume doesn't change the fundamental mechanics. ## Bottom Line Volume explains why **setup costs** (plates, machine calibration) get amortized. It does **not** explain why the raw ink itself is dramatically cheaper, because that comes from **using different ink chemistry and a different transfer method** — not simply "printing more of the same thing."
